content.text:
```json
[
  {
    "name": "Agent Relay",
    "website": "https://agentrelay.com/",
    "yc_batch": "Fall 2026",
    "description": "Lets teams' AI coding agents (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor) message each other directly, with shared searchable session history."
  },
  {
    "name": "Pomerado",
    "website": "https://www.pomerado.ai/",
    "yc_batch": "Fall 2026",
    "description": "Turns any website, legacy portal or internal tool into an API/MCP so agents can use it."
  },
  {
    "name": "Herdr",
    "website": "https://herdr.dev/",
    "yc_batch": "Fall 2026",
    "description": "Open-source server that keeps coding-agent terminal sessions alive and shows which agents are working, blocked or done."
  },
  {
    "name": "Maritime",
    "website": "https://maritime.sh/",
    "yc_batch": "Fall 2026",
    "description": "Managed cloud platform where each AI agent runs in its own isolated, persistent computer."
  },
  {
    "name": "Jcode",
    "website": "https://jcode.sh/",
    "yc_batch": "Summer 2026",
    "description": "High-performance, memory-efficient coding-agent harness for running multi-agent swarms."
  }
]
```

I took these from YC's Developer Tools industry page. Each company's YC profile lists it as "Active" and links to the website above. I picked them by reading the descriptions for agent-focused tools, so they aren't the only matches. The page lists others, such as Mirrors, Agnost AI and Boat.

